-- title:
--   An explicit intertwiner from the sign-twisted staircase cyclic module to words of staircase content
-- statement:
--   Notation: for $n,d\in\mathbb{N}$, $W_{n,d}$ is the space of functions on words $[n]\to[d]$ (with $[d]=\{0,\dots,d-1\}$), on which $S_n$ acts by $(g\cdot x)(a)=x(a\circ g)$, and $\operatorname{sgn}\otimes\rho$ denotes the twist $g\mapsto\operatorname{sgn}(g)\rho(g)$ of a representation $\rho$ of $S_n$ on the same space. For the staircase $\delta_m=\{(i,j):i+j<m\}$, with $n=m(m+1)/2$ cells and $m$ rows, $T$ is its fixed canonical tableau, $T'$ the transposed tableau, $S^T,S^{T'}\subseteq W_{n,m}$ the Specht modules spanned by the orbits of their polytabloids $e_T,e_{T'}$, $C_m\subseteq W_{n,m^2}$ the cyclic module generated by $e_{T'}\otimes e_T$, and $\tau_m$ the repeated target word ($\tau_m(p)=m-1-i$ when $T(p)$ lies in row $i$). Items 2 to 4 take as input an isomorphism of representations $\varphi:S^T\to\operatorname{sgn}\otimes S^{T'}$.
--
--   1. **Word tensor isomorphism.** $W_{n,d}\otimes W_{n,e}\cong W_{n,de}$ as $S_n$-representations (diagonal action on the left), via $x\otimes y\mapsto\bigl((a,b)\mapsto x(a)\,y(b)\bigr)$, where a word over $[d]\times[e]$ is read as a pair of words $(a,b)$.
--   2. **Ambient sign map.** $A_\varphi:W_{n,m}\to\operatorname{sgn}\otimes W_{n,m}$ is the intertwiner
--   $$A_\varphi=\iota_{T'}\circ\varphi\circ\pi_T,$$
--   where $\pi_T:W_{n,m}\to S^T$ is the equivariant orthogonal projection, characterized by $\sum_a(\pi_Tx)(a)\,y(a)=\sum_a x(a)\,y(a)$ for all $y\in S^T$ (it exists because $S^T$ is spanned by real vectors), and $\iota_{T'}$ is the inclusion $S^{T'}\hookrightarrow W_{n,m}$.
--   3. **Pair anti-map.** The intertwiner $\operatorname{sgn}\otimes W_{n,m^2}\to W_{n,m^2}$ obtained by transporting $\mathrm{id}\otimes A_\varphi$ through $W_{n,m^2}\cong W_{n,m}\otimes W_{n,m}$; it acts on the second word of each pair.
--   4. **Dominated quotient map.** The intertwiner $Q_\varphi:\operatorname{sgn}\otimes C_m\to W_{n,m}$,
--   $$Q_\varphi=P_{\tau_m}\circ\Sigma\circ(\mathrm{id}\otimes A_\varphi)\circ\iota_{C_m},$$
--   first includes $C_m$ into $W_{n,m^2}$, applies the pair anti-map, then the letter-sum map $\Sigma$ (sending the basis vector of a pair-word $(a,b)$ to that of $a+b$ when every sum $a(p)+b(p)$ is less than $m$, and to $0$ otherwise), and finally the projection $P_{\tau_m}$ onto the coordinates of the rearrangements of $\tau_m$.
--
--   The image of $Q_\varphi$ is a quotient of $\operatorname{sgn}\otimes C_m$ lying in the permutation module of words with content $(1,2,\dots,m)$. It is used to show that the basis vector $e_{\tau_m}$ lies in this image; combined with Young's rule, this yields nonzero intertwiners from the Specht modules whose shapes are dominated by $\delta_m$ into the cyclic staircase module.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The items are `wordTensorEquiv`, `ambientSignMap m φ`, `pairAntiMap m φ` and `dominatedQuotient m φ`. The projection $\pi_T$ is `subrepProject` applied to the Specht submodule, using that it is closed under complex conjugation; pairs of letters are encoded in `Fin (m*m)` by `finProdFinEquiv`, and the sign twists are handled by `signTwistMap` and `tensorAnti`.
